  <iati-identifier>GB-CHC-202918-MLIB34</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-202918" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam GB</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reversing Land Degradation in Mali by scaling up Evergreen Agriculture</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Just to specify that this project is a continuation of MLIB16. MLIB27 has been created as MLIB16 can&apos;t be extended as the start date of the new Programme Implementation Plan (PIP) it&apos;s linked to is set to January 22 . Otherwise there is no other change between MLIB16 and MLIB27.  The project will be implemented in 2 circles (Koutiala and Yorosso) and will be partnering with 3 other organizations working in different areas and Oxfam, as the lead. We will have a strong partnership with technical services on the ground, working on agriculture, forestry. To achieve our objectives, we will use 2 types of interventions, the Direct and the indirect. The direct will be through our field staff and partners work which will reach 12.500 Households and 50, 000 ha. The indirect will be through our influencing work to engage other actors on the question of regreening. This indirect intervention will then help to get another 7,000 households and 15,000 ha. The main activities will be around building the capacity of farmers, on Trees&apos; production and planting, farmers managing natural regeneration, non timber forest products</narrative>
  </description>
